<!--page {"title": "Idea to Build-Ready: AI-Native Design Sprint · Libre Studio", "description": "An AI-native MVP design sprint for startups: three to six weeks from early idea to a build-ready Figma file, clickable prototype and Cursor-ready handoff.", "path": "/idea-to-build-ready/", "nav": "services"} -->
{{> head}}
{{> nav}}
<main id="main">

  <section class="section hero scheme-dark case-hero" aria-labelledby="sprint-title">
    <div class="container hero__inner">
      <div class="hero__copy">
        <div class="stack">
          <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>AI-native product design sprint</p>
          <h1 class="h1" id="sprint-title" data-split>From idea to a <span class="mark">build-ready<svg class="mark__svg" viewBox="0 0 240 24" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" data-draw><path d="M4 15 C 46 8, 92 19, 136 12 S 210 7, 236 13"/></svg></span> product, in one sprint</h1>
          <p class="text-lg" data-reveal>A fixed-scope product design sprint for startups and founders. In three to six weeks we turn an early-stage idea into a design your developers can build from.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="actions actions--center" data-reveal>
          <a class="btn btn--lime" href="{{calendar}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span class="btn__label"><span data-text="Book a Call">Book a Call</span></span></a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost-dark" href="/work/lula/"><span class="btn__label"><span data-text="See an example">See an example</span></span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <dl class="facts" data-reveal>
        <div><dt>Length</dt><dd>3 to 6 weeks</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Scope</dt><dd>Fixed, agreed before we start</dd></div>
        <div><dt>For</dt><dd>Startups and founders</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Ends with</dt><dd>A build-ready Figma file and handoff</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-light" aria-labelledby="what-title">
    <div class="container split-rows">
      <div class="ai-def">
        <h2 class="h2" id="what-title" data-split>What is the sprint?</h2>
        <div class="text-lg prose" data-reveal>
          <p>An MVP design sprint is a short, fixed-scope engagement that takes a product idea from a brief to a design that is ready to build. Ours runs for three to six weeks and ends with a token-strict Figma file, a clickable prototype and handoff docs your developers can use in Cursor.</p>
          <p>It is AI-native: AI explores wide and fast, and senior designers make every call. The aim is better product decisions, not more screens. Read more about <a class="text-link" href="/ai-design/">how we design with AI</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ai-def">
        <h2 class="h2" id="scope-title" data-split>What can one sprint cover?</h2>
        <div class="text-lg prose" data-reveal>
          <p>An MVP design, one product section such as onboarding, a dashboard or settings, a multi-screen feature flow, or the foundation of a <a class="text-link" href="/design-systems/">design system</a>. We agree the scope on the first call, so you know what you will get before we start.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-coral" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-title narrow">
        <h2 class="h2" id="fit-title" data-split>Is it right for you?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="fit__grid">
        <div class="fit__card fit__card--lime" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="h4">A good fit if you</h3>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"/></svg><span>Have an early-stage idea and need it designed before you build.</span></li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"/></svg><span>Have developers, or will soon, and want a file they can build from.</span></li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"/></svg><span>Need senior product design quickly, without hiring a full team.</span></li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"/></svg><span>Want a fixed scope and a clear end point.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="fit__card fit__card--light" data-reveal>
          <h3 class="h4">Not the right fit if you</h3>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 7v6M12 17h.01"/></svg><span>Mainly need a logo or a brand identity.</span></li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 7v6M12 17h.01"/></svg><span>Need marketing copy written.</span></li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 7v6M12 17h.01"/></svg><span>Want an open-ended design team for months. That is ongoing work, not a sprint.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-light" aria-labelledby="steps-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-title narrow">
        <h2 class="h2" id="steps-title" data-split>What happens during the sprint?</h2>
        <p class="text-lg" data-reveal>The same four steps we use on every project, sized to your scope.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="cycle" data-reveal-group>
        <li class="cycle__step" data-reveal>
          <span class="cycle__num">01</span>
          <h3 class="cycle__title">Strategy</h3>
          <p>We turn your brief into a clear MVP scope: what to build first, and why. See <a class="text-link" href="/product-strategy/">product strategy</a>.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="cycle__step" data-reveal>
          <span class="cycle__num">02</span>
          <h3 class="cycle__title">Design</h3>
          <p>AI explores many directions fast. We choose one, with the reasons written down, then run <a class="text-link" href="/ui-ux-design/">UX, UI</a> and <a class="text-link" href="/prototyping/">prototyping</a> in one loop, with QA before handoff.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="cycle__step" data-reveal>
          <span class="cycle__num">03</span>
          <h3 class="cycle__title">Development</h3>
          <p>A token-strict Figma file, component specs and Cursor-ready handoff docs, walked through with your developers.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="cycle__step" data-reveal>
          <span class="cycle__num">04</span>
          <h3 class="cycle__title">Measure &amp; Optimise</h3>
          <p>A round of questions and answers with your developers after handoff, and a review of what to improve next.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-royal" aria-labelledby="get-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-title narrow">
        <h2 class="h2" id="get-title" data-split>What do you get at the end?</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="checklist ai-get" data-reveal>
        <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"/></svg><span><strong>A build-ready Figma file</strong> on design tokens, named the same as in your code.</span></li>
        <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"/></svg><span><strong>A component library</strong> with spec sheets your developers and their AI tools can read.</span></li>
        <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"/></svg><span><strong>A clickable prototype</strong> of the key flows.</span></li>
        <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"/></svg><span><strong>Cursor-ready handoff docs</strong> and a Loom walkthrough for your developers.</span></li>
        <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"/></svg><span><strong>A decision log</strong>, so the reasons behind the design outlive the sprint.</span></li>
        <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7.5"/></svg><span><strong>One Q&amp;A round</strong> with your developers after handoff.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-light" aria-labelledby="not-title">
    <div class="container split-rows">
      <div class="ai-def">
        <h2 class="h2" id="not-title" data-split>What is not included?</h2>
        <div class="text-lg prose" data-reveal>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Logo and brand identity work.</strong></li>
            <li><strong>Marketing copy.</strong></li>
            <li><strong>User research,</strong> such as interviews. We can add it to the sprint.</li>
            <li><strong>Ongoing iteration after delivery.</strong> That continues as ongoing work if you want it.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-dark" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-title narrow">
        <p class="tagline" data-reveal>Example</p>
        <h2 class="h2" id="proof-title" data-split>Lula: from research to the App Store</h2>
        <p class="text-lg" data-reveal>For <a class="text-link" href="/work/lula/">Lula</a>, an AI bedtime-story app, we went from research to an MVP brief in about a week. The client's developers built the app from our Figma file, and it has been on the App Store since September 2026.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stats stats--3" data-reveal-group>
        <div class="stat" data-reveal><span class="stat__num">6</span><p>specced flows, from onboarding to profile</p></div>
        <div class="stat" data-reveal><span class="stat__num">3</span><p>clickable onboarding prototypes in about two weeks</p></div>
        <div class="stat" data-reveal><span class="stat__num">137</span><p>design tokens as Figma variables</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-light" aria-labelledby="start-title">
    <div class="container split-rows">
      <div class="ai-def">
        <h2 class="h2" id="start-title" data-split>How do we start?</h2>
        <div class="text-lg prose" data-reveal>
          <p><a class="text-link" href="{{calendar}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a call</a> and bring the brief, however messy. If we are a fit, you get time, budget and milestone estimates, then a small demo task before anything is signed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scheme-royal" aria-labelledby="sprint-faq-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-title narrow">
        <h2 class="h2" id="sprint-faq-title" data-split>FAQs</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq__list" data-reveal>
        <details class="faq__item" data-accordion open>
          <summary class="faq__q"><span>How long is the sprint?</span><img class="faq__icon" src="/assets/img/figma/chevron-up.svg" width="32" height="32" alt=""></summary>
          <div class="faq__a" data-accordion-body><div><p>Three to six weeks, depending on the scope we agree on the first call. One product section is shorter than a full MVP.</p></div></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq__item" data-accordion>
          <summary class="faq__q"><span>What do we need to have ready?</span><img class="faq__icon" src="/assets/img/figma/chevron-up.svg" width="32" height="32" alt=""></summary>
          <div class="faq__a" data-accordion-body><div><p>Your idea and whatever you already have: notes, a deck, competitors you admire, an old Figma file. A messy brief is fine. Strategy is the first step of the sprint.</p></div></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq__item" data-accordion>
          <summary class="faq__q"><span>What happens after the sprint?</span><img class="faq__icon" src="/assets/img/figma/chevron-up.svg" width="32" height="32" alt=""></summary>
          <div class="faq__a" data-accordion-body><div><p>Your developers build from the file, with one Q&amp;A round from us. If you want us to keep designing as the product grows, we can continue with ongoing iteration.</p></div></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq__item" data-accordion>
          <summary class="faq__q"><span>Can you also build it?</span><img class="faq__icon" src="/assets/img/figma/chevron-up.svg" width="32" height="32" alt=""></summary>
          <div class="faq__a" data-accordion-body><div><p>The sprint ends with a build-ready design for your developers. If you need more, see <a class="text-link" href="/design-engineering/">design engineering</a>.</p></div></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{> work-next}}
</main>
{{> footer}}
